  "source_audit": "email-source-audit.json",
  "observations": [
    "The committed Chromium adapter fails the first native email image comparison; original images and failed runner logs are retained. The initial Firefox baseline stops at a Marionette NewSession timeout before assertions and establishes no pixel comparison.",
    "The final paired fixtures pass 121 checks/46 complete native images per engine, combining email, plain/password/Unicode and URL/telephone fields. The changed Chromium style reader additionally passes 47 native list checks/15 complete images.",
    "Independent GNUstep keys preserve native Emacs beginning and selection; real-seat Alt+C/V retain original trusted copy/paste/beforeinput/input. Email public selection APIs remain protected before and after edits.",
    "Read-only/disabled fields, native cancellation, inactive script updates, original validation/address sanitization/multiple transitions/maxlength, repeated immediate text/URL/tel/email transitions and native retirement pass.",
    "A focused trace-free Chromium baseline yields x after type change where real GNUstep yields xseed@example.test. Binding eligible fields through the existing before-paint lifecycle fixes this first-key race without waiting for pixels.",
    "Earlier read-only and Alt+A failures were reference assumptions: the original native responder chooses selection, and Alt+A inserts a in that context. Temporary diagnostics are retained and removed from final sources; no UI-library or key-table repair was made.",
    "Both adapter source reproductions are byte-identical to their tested candidates. Twenty production files and current shared loader/provider/shim are unchanged. Descendant renderers retain Seccomp=2/NoNewPrivs=1; no candidate mappings remain after shutdown. Browser binaries were not rebuilt or deployed."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Search/number/date/time/file/color and other specialized webpage controls, richer editing, placeholder/style semantics, IME/accessibility and wider scaling/layout/lifecycle contracts.",
    "Other builds and derivatives, complete detached menus/native shortcuts and installed deployment, followed by GTK/Qt/KDE through the shared native UI library.",
    "Browser toolbar, address bar and tabs keep their existing components; optional future changes belong to app-specific patches."
  ]
